parts=['''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>BTC hourly study — detailed walkthrough</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;background:#f8fafc;color:#18243a}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:42px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1}p{max-width:960px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white;font-size:14px;margin:18px 0}th,td{padding:10px 12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e8f0}th{background:#e2e8f0}.scroll{overflow:auto}a{color:#4338ca}.callout{padding:18px 22px;background:#eef2ff;border-left:4px solid #4338ca}.equation{font-size:20px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.muted{color:#52627a;font-size:14px}img{width:100%;height:auto}details{padding:15px;background:white;margin:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}</style><p class="muted">Explanation of the accepted historical study · 18 October 2026</p><h1>What we predicted, when we entered, and why the account lost money</h1><div class="callout">A correct prediction and a profitable purchase are different measurements. The combined Kalshi signal was correct63.70% of the time, but its average one-contract entry cost including fees was67.27¢ for a contract paying$1 when correct.</div><h2>1. Three prices with different jobs</h2>''']
parts.append(table(['Price','What it means','Example, hypothetical'],[['Market benchmark / strike','The price used to decide the winning side at settlement','$100,000'],['BTC price at entry','Current underlying price; does not replace the market benchmark','$100,400'],['Contract purchase price','What we pay for one YES/NO or UP/DOWN contract','66¢ per contract, plus fees']]))
parts.append('<p>If settlement is $100,100, the Above/Up side wins against a $100,000 benchmark even though BTC fell after a $100,400 entry. For Kalshi KXBTCD, settlement is its final60-second BRTI average compared with the listed strike. For Polymarket hourly Up/Down, settlement compares Binance hourly close with hourly open; equality counts as Up.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>2. The actual early-entry schedule</h2>'+table(['Within the hourly market','Action'],[['Minute0','Identify the exact contract and keep its benchmark fixed.'],['Minute15','Calculate signals using only completed candles; no future minute30 data.'],['Minute16','Modeled fill one minute after the decision, leaving44minutes to expiry.'],['Minute30','Latest permitted entry under the user’s constraint.'],['Minute60','Market expiry and settlement benchmark measurement. Cash arrives at the recorded settlement timestamp, which can be later.']]))
parts.append('<p>Earlier75–77% results used a signal calculated from candles finishing at minute30. A delayed fill would occur at minute31 and violate the new deadline. The compliant decision29 version must use older completed candles: the newest15-minute candle ended at15 and the newest30-minute candle ended at0. Forming-candle indicators were not tested.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>3. Exactly how the two indicators vote</h2>'+table(['Component','Kalshi selected settings','Polymarket selected settings','Directional vote'],[['Stochastic','15m chart;67lookback, K=1, D=1','15m chart;62lookback, K=1, D=1','Rising D → +1; falling D → −1; flat →0.'],['SMA crossover','45m chart;SMA2 crossing SMA3','Same','Fresh upward cross →+1; downward cross →−1; no fresh cross →0.']]))
parts.append('<p>Stochastic measures the close’s position inside its lookback high–low range. With K/D smoothing set to1, K and D are identical. This selected rule uses the line’s slope, not an overbought/oversold threshold. SMA uses2and3candles, not calendar days. The45-minute candles follow fixed UTC boundaries; a new candle does not close at minute15 in every hour.</p>')
parts.append(table(['Stochastic vote','SMA vote','Action'],[['Up','Up or no fresh cross','Predict Up/Above'],['Down','Down or no fresh cross','Predict Down/Below'],['Up','Down','Skip'],['Down','Up','Skip'],['Flat','Fresh Up or Down cross','Follow the fresh SMA cross'],['Flat','No fresh cross','Skip']]))
parts.append('<p><strong>This is a voting strategy, not a requirement that both indicators independently confirm every trade.</strong> When the SMA has no fresh crossover, the stochastic can supply the only active vote.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>4. Results with at least30minutes remaining</h2>');rows=[]
for off in (0,15,29):
 row=[off,off+1,60-off-1]
 for venue in ('Kalshi','Polymarket'):
  m=results[venue]['selected'][f'mixed_combination/offset{off}']['evaluation'];row.append(f"{m['wins']}/{m['active']} = {pct(m['accuracy'])}")
 rows.append(row)
