parts.append('<p>Each row has separately selected settings. Minute16 was the overall choice for both targets because selection used validation correlation, which accounts for coverage—not whichever later evaluation row had the highest win rate. Kalshi’s minute30 version won66.54% on532signals, while minute16 won63.70% on774signals. Its validation correlation was0.304 versus0.326for the chosen minute16 version. The full results retain both.</p>')
parts.append('<p>The minute16 strategy also failed to improve on a simple price comparison. On comparable active hours, latest observed BTC price versus the market benchmark scored65.72% for Kalshi and65.22% for Polymarket, compared with the combined signals’ approximately63.7–63.8%. One exact-price tie makes Kalshi’s comparison denominator773instead of774; the paired difference is−1.94percentage points.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>5. A profitable win rate depends on entry cost</h2><p>Use the equal-size reference: buy one contract on every one of the774eligible Kalshi signals, ignoring account depletion. These are historical quotes and modeled fees, not actual fills.</p>')
parts.append(table(['All774signals, one contract each','Amount'],[['Correct outcomes / payout','493 × $1 = $493.00'],['Total purchase prices',cash(premium)],['Total modeled fees',cash(fees)],['Net result',cash(net)],['Average purchase price','65.842¢'],['Average fee','1.429¢'],['Average all-in cost / break-even win rate','67.271¢ / 67.271%'],['Actual signal win rate','63.695%'],['Average net per contract','−3.576¢']]))
parts.append('<p class="equation">$493.00 − $509.62 − $11.06 = −$27.68</p><p>Prices and fees varied by signal. The67.271¢ figure is their average, not a fixed price on every trade. This calculation uses one equal-sized contract per signal; it does not describe the variable-size$500account. For a hypothetical contract costing67¢ all-in, a win earns33¢ while a loss loses67¢. Counting wins alone hides that asymmetry.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>6. The first six trades from the actual paper ledger</h2><p>All times below are America/New_York (EDT). YES means Above the listed strike; NO wins when the greater-than condition is false. Each trade uses at most25%of the settled balance, including fees, with integer contracts.</p>');rows=[]
