parts.append(table(['Full finite account','Result'],[['Active signals','774'],['Trades account could fund','283'],['Skipped because25%budget could not buy one contract','491'],['Wins / losses','178 /105'],['Trade win rate','62.90%'],['Contracts bought','5,931'],['Winning contracts / total contracts','3,175 /5,931 =53.53%'],['Total premiums over repeated trading','$3,584.74'],['Total payouts','$3,175.00'],['Total fees','$89.6626'],['Net loss','$499.4026'],['Ending cash','$0.5974']]))
parts.append('<p>Different trades bought different numbers of contracts, so62.90%winning trades does not mean62.90%of purchased contracts won. The contract-weighted win rate was53.53%. Sizing at25%of current cash also compounds the path: a losing trade removes roughly a quarter of the then-current balance, and the next allocation is based on the reduced balance. Recoveries occurred—the balance rose from$25.89after50trades to$144.02after100—but the account later depleted.</p><p>Before fees, payouts minus premiums already lost$409.74. Fees added$89.6626. The loss was not caused by fees alone. The single-contract calculation also lost money, so the problem is not solely the25%allocation.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>8. What this does and does not establish</h2><p>This tests prediction of each market’s official benchmark outcome, with an entry deadline and completed candles. It does not forecast BTC’s exact closing dollar price. It does not establish profitable incremental value over the simple current-price comparison.</p><p>Evaluation:September13–October17,2026, a35-day period already inspected in earlier research. These are exploratory results. Daily-block95%interval for the equal-contract mean net runs approximately−7.05¢to+0.11¢; the observed loss is not proof of permanently negative expected value. Quotes model full fills without historical depth/queue proof. No executable Polymarket ask history was established, so its profit is unverified.</p><p>This explanation adds no new strategy selection, data collection, or account replay. It derives directly from accepted outputs and ledgers. All original research files remain unchanged.</p><p><a href="../report.html">Full early-entry research report</a> · <a href="../accounts/mixed/delayed_close/trades.jsonl">Exact283-trade ledger</a> · <a href="../paper-results.json">Paper results</a> · <a href="evidence.json">Explanation evidence and source hashes</a></p><p>Official terms: <a href="https://assets.kalshi.com/contract_terms/BTC.pdf">Kalshi BTC contract</a> · <a href="https://polymarket.com/event/bitcoin-up-or-down-october-1-2026-7am-et">Polymarket hourly rules</a>.</p></html>')
